# Base URL of the Remy backend HTTP API (no trailing slash).
#
# Leave commented out in dev: the default "/api/v1" plus Vite's server.proxy
# forward everything to the local NestJS backend at localhost:3000. Same-origin
# means no CORS headaches and no need to tunnel the backend separately.
#
# Override in production with an absolute URL, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.remy.example.com/api/v1
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
